<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank - has no plans to raise capital.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank - has no plans to raise capital.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerzbank AG said on Friday it had no concrete plans to increase its capital even though it was asking shareholders for approval to create authorised capital.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no concrete plans for a capital increase,&quot; chief executive Martin Kohlhaussen told the group's annual shareholders meeting.</p>
<p>He said Commerzbank aimed to increase its core capital ratio to six percent by the year 2000 from 5.2 percent now and aimed to do this by accumulating retained earnings if possible.</p>
<p>--David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
